PAGE RISKS (builder handoff, judged from the page specs)

- Door pages: the builder said three pages show a girl at an open door. A case-insensitive grep for "door" in docs/storytime/l2-unit1/w05/ finds TWO specs, not three: pam-is-off-sam (Nan full body in the door opening) and pam-is-on-sam (only one sneaker and one leg step in at the right edge). Both colorPrompts are clear: each names the door to draw as a plain wooden door frame with a plain open door at the right. The set picture has no door, so the model must add it. Advice: at page review, check exactly one door at the right with a clear opening, and no second window shape.
- Leg-only page: pam-is-on-sam carries a strong guard. It names only one small white sneaker and one bare child leg up to a hint of red shorts, cropped by the picture edge, and lists no body, no arms, no head, no face. The prompt is clear enough. Advice: at page review, check that no head, torso, or arm of Nan appears.
- Nose page tail: i-have-one-nose states that ONLY the fluffy golden-brown tail sticks out behind the tree trunk, and lists no puppy head, no puppy body, no puppy legs. The wording is clear. The gap is different: this page has no Pip picture in its references, so the model must build the tail from text alone. Advice: at page review, check one closed fluffy tail shape that ends on the tree trunk line and no other puppy part; if the tail reads wrong, add the Pip render and re-run.

